\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Verified an explicit noncommuting unitary braid representation and used it to test scalar-loop generalization; no microscopic anyon construction.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30004242. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{A nonabelian braid diagnostic.} On \(\mathbb C^2\) define
\[
 B_1=\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&i\end{pmatrix},\quad
 H=2^{-1/2}\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&-1\end{pmatrix},\quad B_2=HB_1H.
\]
All three matrices are unitary. Direct multiplication gives
\[
 B_1B_2B_1=B_2B_1B_2=\frac{1+i}{2}\begin{pmatrix}1&1\\1&-1\end{pmatrix}.
\]
Thus \(B_1,B_2\) represent the two generators of the three-strand braid group. They do not commute: their upper-right entries in \(B_1B_2\) and \(B_2B_1\) are respectively \((1-i)/2\) and \((1+i)/2\). Replacing each transport by a scalar phase cannot retain this fusion-space action.
\paragraph{Attempted microscopic interpretation.} The algebra is a necessary diagnostic for any proposed nonabelian construction: transport operations must act on a space of dimension greater than one and their ordering matters. But these matrices specify no lattice support, local Hamiltonian, spectral gap or protected excitation subspace. An arbitrary embedding of \(\mathbb C^2\) into a many-body Hilbert space would still not provide path-local loop operators or deformation invariance.
\paragraph{Gap and audit.} The first missing step is constructing localized microscopic transport whose compressed operators satisfy the braid relation with controlled errors and the source's gap/locality assumptions. Closing a path and proving the resulting loop detects the appropriate charge are further tasks. This exact small braid representation is familiar auxiliary algebra, not a microscopic realization and not a solution of the source abelian-to-nonabelian extension.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Multiplied both braid words and checked noncommutation and unitarity; kept an abstract representation distinct from local microscopic loops. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Multiplied both braid words and checked noncommutation and unitarity; kept an abstract representation distinct from local microscopic loops. The remaining gap is: Construct local charge transport in an admissible gapped microscopic Hamiltonian and prove its protected fusion-space action. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the two explicit matrix products, unitarity and noncommutation; no microscopic realization follows from the braid representation. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file-reading/writing tools for manuscript serialization and structural checks; mathematical calculations were symbolic reasoning, with no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Construct local charge transport in an admissible gapped microscopic Hamiltonian and prove its protected fusion-space action.

